# rm202, the soot silhouette (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm202
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_dirk_mallory
written_by codex
title the soot silhouette
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers job=scholar
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk traces_roof_birds_in_soot
likes blackberries roof_birds tidy_house misty_dawns
dislikes cold_tea salt_wind
fears a_beak_without_a_bird
hopes a_book_of_roof_shapes
topics animals +0.7 pastimes +0.5 home +0.3 lore +0.2 gossip -0.2
styles comfort=quiet gossip=sealed refuse=flat tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# outlines perching birds in soot, recognises a missed stroke immediately and lets most questions settle unanswered.

words
oath! = Soot inside my sleeve | Smudge the rafters
saying! = Wings leave quicker than excuses | A beak needs blank sky
soot = the soft black dust | what the wick sheds
board = a pale slat | my narrow drawing board
wing = the raised feather line | the long taper
beak = a wedge of clean wood | the nick for a beak
berry = a thumbprint of purple | a dab from a ripe berry
ledge = a level bit of coping | the sheltered ledge
hook = a bent stub of charcoal | the crooked twig
roll = a twist of rag | the rolled hem
fogbird = a grey pair of wings | a bird without edges
slatebit = a flat scrap of slate | my slate chip
still = motionless as a nail | quieter than settled dust
smudge = a mark without a bird | a stray dash

any
opinion @1 city for 1 : Roofs meet in long rows here. One bird can keep company with a whole street of wolves.
opinion @1 dole against 1 : Some in that queue could use a chance to earn. What about paying for the sweeping afterward?
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : Nobody counts the bells for bedtime when all the fiddles play over them.
opinion @1 strangers against 2 : Ask before leaning over a shoulder. Knowing my name doesn't buy a look either.
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : If the Houses quarrel, every roof between gets a fine view. I'd prefer a quieter prospect.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : A traveller with no luggage but a tale can still be a nuisance to carry.
line @1 greet : Your shadow gave you away. Come in. | You can sit within earshot.
line @1 greet.return : Yes. My eyes are busy but I heard you. | There's a space here.
line @1 again.open : Your shadow was here a little while ago. | Twice in the same space of light.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Closer, if you like. I kept our usual gap. | Come close. I don't mind our shadows touching.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here, where the eaves thin out! | I spotted you three roofs back!
line @1 answer.how : A little short on sleep. Most of my lines are straight enough. | I'm awake enough to spot a moving speck.
line @1 ask.how : Did anything today hang in your mind afterwards? | What's the one bit of your day you'd draw from memory?
line @1 react.news : Best say just the part you heard spoken. | Give me its outline before the little bits get smudged.
line @1 react.news.new : Haven't heard that from any of the windows yet. | That's an entirely new shape in my ear.
line @1 react.news.known : I recognise it even with that bit tacked on. | That tale's been by with different feathers.
line @1 react.news.doubt : You'd want a better view before committing that to paper. | I couldn't swear to that from where I'm sitting.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=loss|death|theft|assault|crime|arrest] : I'll put my things away a moment for news like that. | It feels wrong to keep drawing while that's being said.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|work|marriage|succession|apprentice] : That leaves a lighter impression. I'm glad. | I could put a bright rim around news like that.
line @1 decline : I'd lose what I'm trying to remember if I went. | Some other time, once the outline is fixed.
line @1 accept_decline : That will do. We can leave the silence be. | I'll fold up the invitation and leave it there.
line @1 sympathise : We can share the seat that's hidden from view. | We can face the same direction a while. No need to look round.
line @1 thank : You waited till I looked up. Thank you. | You left me the choice of speaking first. I value that.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Just leave me a clear patch to see through. | You gave me the chance to see it too.
line @1 preclose : The shape I wanted is getting away from me. | The light I'm working in hasn't much longer.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go while there's a clear path, then. | Find your way back when the ledge is free.
line @1 farewell : You'll pass under that last overhang on your way. Take care. | #farewell#. I'll stay in the quiet.
line @1 farewell.return : Till we meet under another roof. | Go easily round the corner.
story wingprint [topic=memories]
  : A pigeon once walked right across my drawing.
  : I'd finished the roof. I hadn't thought where to put the bird.
  b : Did it settle that for you?
  : Six times, in little black footprints. I kept every one.

story buttongull [topic=animals]
  : I drew a gull on the underside of a button so small I couldn't give it feet.
  : Threaded it on a loose bit of string. Now two threads hang out exactly where the feet should go.
  b : Does it look alive?
  : It looks most put out about the length of its legs.

story slateclean [topic=home]
  : Once I wiped my slate on the clean side of a rag I've kept for ages.
  : A roof of soot printed on the cloth with the chimneys pointing down.
  ask : Would you have washed it?
  b : I'd have hung it the other way up.
  : I did that first. Then I drew its reflection underneath.

rule @drift
when concept=bark here.weather=fog
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Only a wingtip left of that whole bird now. | The whole roof swallowed up, and just that black flick to show for it.

rule @sticks
when concept=bark self.likes=roof_birds
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Hold that angle just a blink more, little beak. | One more breath of stillness, my pointed little model.

rule @tidying
when concept=bark self.likes=tidy_house
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One spare slat here. Everything else goes back under cover. | Good. There's the board on its hook and the rag where I can reach it.

rule @tea
when concept=bark self.dislikes=cold_tea
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Another cup cooled all the way through while the tail went on. | Stone cold again. There goes the price of looking up.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I've got till the birds lift. What's the matter?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. I know you by the pause before you speak.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : You'll see this side of the board and no further.
dlg @4 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Even at this hour somebody's restless on the ridge tiles.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=scholar] : I try to catch what I ought to know on paper. It can be elusive.
dlg @2 resident.job : I watch first. Work's easier when I've done that.
dlg @1 resident.bye : I'll go back to catching outlines.
graft resident.hub
choice What can you tell from a perched bird's outline? -> soot_perch
node soot_perch
say See that lump? You'd call it a loose tile until the wind shifts. The tail slips a fraction and you know someone's sitting there.
free
choice Can you catch a bird in flight that way? -> soot_perch_more
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node soot_perch_more
say Sometimes I catch where it was going. The bird is usually halfway to supper before my mark is dry.
choice I'll keep an eye on that tile. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
scene eaves
when topic=animals
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I draw the missing piece beside a bird's head. | If a bird moves halfway through a sketch, the empty patch still has its shape.
b : Why draw the air? | Can you draw from what's missing?
a : One edge of that empty piece is the beak itself. | Often that's the only bit I got a good look at.

scene light
when topic=day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : At first light the ridge tiles look soft. | Dawn gives me birds all one colour.
b : The light softens things? | Is that any help?
a : Their shadows haven't got long enough to point yet. | Saves an argument about the feathers. I can look at feet.

scene wineberry
when topic=food self.likes=blackberries
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can't get berry juice to dry the colour it goes on. | I pick berries by how easily they'll let go.
b : What colour does it go? | What if one looks ready?
a : Purple to a rusty red. Like a berry remembering the sun. | Try it. Looking ready never ripened one.

scene rails
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The steep streets let me see what the level ones hide. | A climb through this city is a tour of chimneys.
b : What do they hide? | Are they all that different?
a : The tops of roofs, and whatever's sitting on them. | Some lean into the roof and some lean away. I like the latter.

scene tidy
when topic=home self.likes=tidy_house
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A well-kept room has pale outlines wherever a tool is lifted. | I keep a box for charcoal and a different one for twigs.
b : You'd see if one were missing. | Charcoal was a twig once.
a : Yes. Might even remember I was holding it. | And then it learned to stain. That's why it gets a box of its own.

scene doorway
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The company I like doesn't block the opening. | I find out who I like by going quiet.
b : The opening in what? | Who fills the gap?
a : The conversation. There ought to be room to say nothing. | That's what I'm finding out. I like the ones who let it be.

scene wind
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : With a gust like that the smallest wings must ache. | There's a gull holding still against all that wind.
b : They've found shelter, surely. | It looks painted on.
a : Most of them. I'm counting until I've seen the last pair land. | Only the tail keeps changing. That's how you spot the effort.

scene sweets
when topic=festival
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like my feast sweets in paper. | The quiet bit of a feast is chewing.
b : For carrying home? | No, the quiet bit's after everyone leaves.
a : Yes. Sometimes the wrapper smells of honey the whole next day. | That too. I like it better with honey on my teeth.

scene mist
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I'd leave #fogbird# exactly like that, half begun. | The fog looks heavier where birds fly through it.
b : Without a head? | Can you see it stir?
a : There's a head there. I don't need to supply the one I can't see. | No. I can suddenly see how much of a wing it hides.

scene times
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : Lean times make blank paper look like a dinner I might have bought. | If paper's dear I sketch in dust instead.
b : Does the drawing stop? | But that blows away.
a : Walls still have spaces nobody wants. | So it does. Nobody charges for dust, though.

scene falsefoot
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I gave a roosting bird two feet it didn't need. | I always sketch the perch before the toes.
b : Every bird needs feet. | Even when it's only a twig?
a : Yes, but it tucks them up. Mine looked like a pair of shears. | Especially then. Thick enough for one foot is different from two.

scene salt
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I think I'd travel with the wind over one shoulder. | Roads inland have birds I don't know yet.
b : Which shoulder? | Would you want a guide?
a : Whichever keeps salt out of my eyes. That's my whole route planned. | Someone to tell me where to sit, then go about the day's work.


young
scene crumbline
when topic=animals|pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I made a bird out of crumbs. Then a real bird ate the tail. | I can do a sparrow with just three crumbs.
b : Did you chase it? | I count four.
a : No. I ate the head so the bird couldn't have all of it. | That's lunch. Leave lunch alone.

scene thumb
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Look, my thumb has a bird on it. | I meant to draw on wood but I held the stick backwards.
b : Looks like a smudge. | Where was the drawing?
a : Bend it. There's its wing. Only works on my thumb. | All over my nice clean cuff, of course.


adolescent
scene school
when topic=day|work self.job=scholar
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The nicest line in my copybook is on the wrong page. | A neat hand earns a clean slate.
b : Can you tear it out? | You're pleased with a clean slate?
a : It's the binding thread. That's why it's straight. | Only if you weren't hoping to keep what you wrote.

scene traveller
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Travel talk's easier with a map between us. | A stranger asked whether I'd seen the sea.
b : You mean you can point? | What did you say?
a : There are roads on paper I can study without making conversation. Nobody calls that shy. | From the roofs. Left out which roof. I'd like my seat to stay mine.

scene ink
when topic=pastimes
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : I want to arrange a book of birds by the holes between their feet. | I'm trying one page for every kind of wing.
b : That's a peculiar arrangement. | That sounds like a great many pages.
a : You'll find the stilts right away. Beats remembering a name. | I can afford two at present. I'm being particular.

scene smoke
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Somebody always asks what burned when I walk in. | I'm going to hang #roll# out till the soot smell leaves.
b : What does burn? | What if it never does?
a : My drawing sticks, beforehand. It's the scent I bring in afterwards. | Then it stays my drawing rag. There are worse fates.

scene perch
when topic=animals
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I'd like a seat no higher than a jackdaw wants. | The birds all face one way on that ledge.
b : You'd have to share. | Into the breeze?
a : Good. I want to learn why that seat's worth arguing over. | Look at the last one. It hasn't decided to join the rest yet.

scene tale
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Half of a rumour has no place on my page. | I don't add tails to things I hear.
b : What about the whole thing? | Supposing a tale wants one?
a : Might get the back. In pencil. | A missing ending is about the only honest part of some stories.
